'''''Cynara humilis''''', called '''wild thistle''', is a species of flowering plant in the artichoke and cardoon genus ''[[Cynara]]'' native to Portugal, Spain, Morocco, Algeria and [[Gran Canaria]], in the Canary Islands.<ref name="200890-1" >{{cite web |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:200890-1 |title=''Cynara humilis'' L. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2017 |website=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Board of Trustees of the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew |access-date=3 November 2020 }}</ref> It is used locally as a coagulant in artisanal sheep and goat cheesemaking.<ref>{{cite journal |doi=10.1046/j.1471-0307.2003.00080.x |title=Cheesemaking with vegetable coagulants-the use of ''Cynara'' L. for the production of ovine milk cheeses |year=2003 |last1=Roseiro |first1=Luisa Bivar |last2=Barbosa |first2=Manuela |last3=Ames |first3=Jennifer M. |last4=Wilbey |first4=R Andrew |journal=International Journal of Dairy Technology |volume=56 |issue=2 |pages=76–85 |doi-access=free }}</ref>

